# Catalog signing trust root for agents content cuts (#2082).
#
# OpenSSH allowed_signers format. Principal `catalog@battlelab`, namespace `battlelab-plugins`.
# A key listed here may sign AGENTS CONTENT CUTS ONLY (`plugin-feed.json`), checked by
# `feed.verify` after the release key (`feed-signers`) and with the same sequence floor, rollback
# and equivocation rules. Nothing else reads this file: not the gallery, not freshness statements,
# not release tags. Every line carries `namespaces="battlelab-plugins"` so the key verifies nothing
# outside that namespace even where this file is misused.
#
# Adding a line grants an unattended signer the authority to approve agent recipes, i.e. binaries
# that hosts install and update on their own. Removing it revokes that for every build shipped
# afterwards. Held by the relay's signer (battlelab-cloud#98). Public key material only.
#
# One key since #2082 activation: the operator approved the grant on #2082 (comment 139389,
# 2026-11-24) and the key was generated on the relay VM the same day, root-only behind the signer's
# own identity (SHA256:AihNywtlvKDeA8qgFy/DIaB+nwtL4As0GpksFVwNwS8; custody in
# docs/release-signing.md). Recovery and rollout: docs/invariants/agent-catalog.md.
catalog@battlelab namespaces="battlelab-plugins" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIAepryiQbXYi+Y2df0rKb1y9a9HLek5uujOJPMIPGYPj
